<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Amnesty says Iran committed 'crimes against humanity' in 2022 protests crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df36891ca1ccae46523bb42aa451f3e9eaf9b2931b1d72dc97af6b560ef0b155</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:30:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-amnesty-international-says-iran-committed-crimes-against-humanity-in-2022-protests-crackdown" /><summary type="html">In a report released Wednesday, Amnesty International said Iranian authorities committed “crimes against humanity” during the violent crackdown on the 2022 protests known as the movement “Woman, Life, Freedom” that was sparked by the death of Mahsa Amini.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Arab League chief condemns alleged Houthi attack on Mecca</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2138b538318570688389e7785b1f6109a5d89adfe4f5bf0916b0d835c189073d</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T02:14:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-middle-east-live-saudi-arabia-accuses-houthi-rebels-of-launching-a-drone-strike-on-mecca--9e1fb82fa78e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260916-middle-east-live-saudi-arabia-accuses-houthi-rebels-of-launching-a-drone-strike-on-mecca" /><summary type="html">The Secretary General of the Arab League, Nabil Fahmy, condemned on Wednesday the alleged Houthi attack on Mecca.He spoke after the Saudi-led coalition battling Yemen's Houthis accused rebels of targeting Islam's holy city Mecca, sparking outrage across the Muslim world and deepening the conflict roiling the region. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi crown prince seeks neighbours' backing as Houthi attacks rattle Red Sea oil routes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d3880fa4b5ef82987a9461a36e7bf22a65329b81497bc356aec0ca6fdc2ab87</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T18:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-crown-prince-seeks-neighbours-backing-as-houthi-attacks-rattle-red-sea-oil-routes--7b79977cbb18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/saudi-crown-prince-seeks-neighbours-backing-as-houthi-attacks-rattle-red-sea-oil-routes" /><summary type="html">Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman and Egyptian President Abdel Fattah al-Sisi called for free and secure navigation in the Red Sea during talks in Cairo on Tuesday, as the kingdom vowed to respond "firmly" to attacks by Yemen's Houthis. The two regional powers discussed the threat posed by the Iran-backed group's control over the Bab al-Mandab Strait. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>First Hormuz, now the Red Sea? Oil spikes as Saudis sucked into Yemen spiral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:414b822fd42db2f7facc8e873a5ab4e6222b0984a3390a8390f6a495006a0d13</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T18:32:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260915-first-hormuz-now-the-red-sea-oil-spikes-as-saudis-sucked-into-yemen-spiral--9f0622b7393d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260915-first-hormuz-now-the-red-sea-oil-spikes-as-saudis-sucked-into-yemen-spiral" /><summary type="html">First, there was US President Donald Trump’s surprise decision to strike Iran. Then, came the quagmire of a war without an exit strategy. Now, six months later, with access to the Strait of Hormuz all but shut, global shipping has taken another hit the other end of the Arabian Peninsula. Iran-backed Houthis are threatening access to the Red Sea.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia vows to hit back ‘firmly’ after Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ae5fc9d3a79745da42fe6e09a006c738021fbd7db861d4ebeae348e503c6523</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T03:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia--99d547e8fe8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia vowed on Tuesday to respond "firmly" to attacks by Yemen's Houthis after the Iran-backed fighters wounded 13 people in the kingdom’s south following a series of drone and missile attacks. Tensions have escalated since the Houthis pushed their offensive in Yemen and began targeting Riyadh’s ships in the Red Sea. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Rights group accuses Israel of dismantling 'Palestinian existence' in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b16f86974897f963ac7f0ebb564bb2bc79dda2fb3aa07a09e1a9a522eb7238f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:26:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank--bd6f33b37af6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli rights group B'Tselem said Monday that Israeli actions in the occupied West Bank form part of a greater project designed to make it impossible for Palestinians to exist together as a people. In a report titled "The Elimination Project", the group alleged five connected Israeli tactics and policies in the West Bank: "violence, ethnic cleansing, movement restrictions, economic strangulation, social and political destruction". FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fact-checking videos claiming to show Houthi rebel attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e21889a74ad235efcd20139d86fe57926e5adce4cce9c24002b056f7faf8271c</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1--aba5070fd86a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1" /><summary type="html">A video claiming to show Houthi rebels ambushing Saudi-backed mercenaries has racked up major views on X. But the FRANCE 24 Observers found it is actually footage of 2024 Houthi military drills. The clip was edited with football commentary and blurred flags, which originally show Israel, the UK and US, not Saudi Arabia. Other viral videos falsely linked to Houthi attacks on a Saudi Aramco refinery were also traced to unrelated fires in Texas and Russia. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Axis of Iranian centrality' remains "one of more destabilising forces in the region", expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8fcc992d77887253f7e1a95e555fc2b08a080567f9b5fcf4761fc8f87ac39c8</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:46:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says--6f7fe028932a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis launched a fresh barrage of missile and drone attacks on Saudi military targets on Monday, as Iran denied any involvement in the country's revived civil war. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr H. A. Hellyer, Senior Fellow in Geopolitics, International Security, and Middle East Studies at the Royal United Services Institute, says that Iran and its non-state proxies "remain to be one of the more destabilising forces in the region alongside the Israeli project of regional paramountcy".</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis and Saudi Arabia renew fighting, Iran denies any interference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9395319411d877e3a07957f8fb2d15263f0bea801e7ca8854d369a820ac73204</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:05:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-houthis-and-saudi-arabia-renew-fighting-iran-denies-any-interference--5a342294d627.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-houthis-and-saudi-arabia-renew-fighting-iran-denies-any-interference" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes on western Yemen on Monday after Iran-backed Houthi rebels attacked military facilities in the kingdom. The renewed fighting around the Red Sea comes as the wider US-Iran war threatens vital shipping routes across the region.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Who is Iran's 'influential spymaster' Hossein Taeb and does he pull the strings?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c000ce5bda7c01f1f4c39e4fe1687370a5bae9e3337e59a04e586ff10c9bc522</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:40:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260914-who-is-iran-s-influential-spymaster-hossein-taeb-and-does-he-pull-the-strings--bd37a8a17fa2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260914-who-is-iran-s-influential-spymaster-hossein-taeb-and-does-he-pull-the-strings" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 14: The New York Times released an exclusive report titled “How Iran’s hard-liners prevailed and sabotaged the US peace deal”. Also: Trump says AI fears are "exaggerated", but reports show a different reality.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'open' to holding talks with Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d50096c529ba4371750e2032477c72792ff09c06b0e06e81e473a9165761ed2a</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T03:39:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces--255384c3850b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Monday he is willing to negotiate with Iran, after weeks of saying it was too early to make a deal with Tehran to end the Middle East war. "The failing Nation of Iran wants to make a deal, quickly and badly. I will determine whether or not the USA will choose to engage – the concept of which we are open to," Trump said on his Truth Social network. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian cargo vessel struck near Qeshm Island as Oman delays Tehran-Gulf talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff459ed5eb89954faad1564e7d1d9443a638513dde91a9b36419734bb591a4c</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T02:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-iranian-ship-qeshm-island-tehran-hormuz--6f35a399668f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260914-iranian-ship-qeshm-island-tehran-hormuz" /><summary type="html">An Iranian cargo vessel was struck off Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz on Sunday, killing one person and wounding four, Iranian state media said. Tehran blamed a “terrorist enemy” for the attack, which came as threats to shipping intensified around the Hormuz and Bab el-Mandeb straits.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Sucker Punch: How the Houthis shocked the Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcb692bce94fb7f0368bf3fcee36703bbfa5b62942362f24a938984dc15f8d4c</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sucker-punch-how-the-houthis-shocked-the-gulf--61120806097f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sucker-punch-how-the-houthis-shocked-the-gulf" /><summary type="html">Who are the Houthis, what are their objectives for Yemen, and could the Iranian-backed group hold a significant part of world trade to ransom in the Bab el Mandeb Strait?
 
FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks with Professor Thomas Juneau, a specialist on the Houthis and Iran, explains the intricate dynamics of the group, its repressive nature and the level of the threat to world shipping.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: The Houthis test Iran's regional influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edf02406fec6c37043363a20175cb69e5e89f013b351d87b8190eb07d18020f1</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:29:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence--0d58b065c31c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia have intensified as fighting spreads around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a vital chokepoint for global trade and oil shipments. On FRANCE 24, Sanaa Center for Strategic Studies chairman Farea Al-Muslimi argued this could mark "the last round in Yemen's current war", unpacking the Houthis' ties with Iran and the growing pressure on Washington as the group targets US allies while Donald Trump heads into a crucial election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting escalates around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5ac394a686e268b638860d37708452dd3fb8ac788aeb023b2bcfc67131f1125</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait--21a715d75bc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait" /><summary type="html">Fighting is escalating in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi forces seized strategic territory around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, prompting counterstrikes by government forces and reported Saudi air raids. The Houthis also claimed attacks inside southern Saudi Arabia and threatened to disrupt shipping through the key maritime chokepoint, raising fears for regional security and global trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi offensive triggers new displacement crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:199f0bb010ebf28e74cc9e38a0fbaf161f5e675099d3d7ad86a9a765aa070fa0</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis--a8dbf0351ee1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis" /><summary type="html">More than 70,000 people have fled their homes in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi rebels launched an offensive to seize the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, with many escaping to Aden and around 1,400 crossing into neighbouring Djibouti. The UN and IOM warn the new displacement wave is worsening an already dire humanitarian crisis in a country devastated by 12 years of war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis say hit Saudi base amid renewed fighting with Yemeni forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97540d0a96da96eb3c9cc5ea0064da8147942f0695f86a0f35de56dc9af3414d</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T05:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces--c82714ec875f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces" /><summary type="html">Yemeni Houthi rebels claimed responsibility on Sunday for an attack on a military base in southern Saudi Arabia as renewed fighting with Yemen's government forces forced growing numbers of civilians to flee. Fighting in western Yemen over the past few weeks has left hundreds dead and displaced tens of thousands of people. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia closes East-West pipeline as Houthis tighten grip on Red Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e10c2d859f6e377cf000e5e5453d6188917c74ca71675ff23f197469e374f1f2</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T20:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea--fb1623bbcd35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia on Saturday ​shut down the vital East-West pipeline after the conduit came under attack in the widening Middle East war, threatening to send energy prices soaring. The 1,200-km pipeline has served as the main route out for global ​supplies of Middle East oil for the ‌past six months while the Strait of Hormuz has been largely shut by war.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Has Trump Left MBS hanging over Yemen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c35fe4ce1209864d96d3c28738843373cb95b4550a88bde9747d5755a298a7e</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T18:49:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260912-has-trump-left-mbs-hanging-over-yemen--bd72ea395246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260912-has-trump-left-mbs-hanging-over-yemen" /><summary type="html">The Yemeni and Saudi governments are under pressure. The Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed Bin Salman reportedly called US President Donald Trump twice to ask him to authorise US strikes against the Houthis in Yemen over the threat to the Bab el Mandeb Strait. According to Axios, the US President declined. FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee discusses that decision and the wider conflict with  the retired Lieutenant General Ben Hodges, former commander of US ground forces in Europe, and former Commander of NATO Allied Land Command in Izmir, Turkey.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Jewish ‘supercop’ runs on Arab ticket in Israeli polls – and sparks a storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd4d4595e9c88e7cfe4d6cd6f1a95c790c7887a7fc67655bb64be2ad28315410</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:50:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-jewish-supercop-runs-on-arab-ticket-in-israeli-polls-_-and-sparks-a-storm--78a4e19f8357.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-jewish-supercop-runs-on-arab-ticket-in-israeli-polls-%E2%80%93-and-sparks-a-storm" /><summary type="html">Former Israeli police officer Yoav Segalovitz's decision to run as the No. 2 candidate on the Arab Raam party ticket in the October 2026 elections marks a paradigm change in Israeli politics. Far-right politicians have slammed the move, but it could pave the way for an Arab party to join a coalition opposing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his allies.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran got Chinese satellite images before deadly strike on US troops, report reveals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01f29e24658ee603696c4d3e5ce3e9eae972b5a7655e43249d2b51f726e25d1f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-live-saudi-arabia-oil-pipeline-shut-down-after-drone-attack-launched-from-iraq--71db50b1fb89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-live-saudi-arabia-oil-pipeline-shut-down-after-drone-attack-launched-from-iraq" /><summary type="html">A report released by The Wall Street Journal on Saturday said Chinese entities supplied Iran with satellite images of a base in Jordan before and after an attack that killed three US soldiers. US President Donald Trump has warned Beijing not to sell weapons to Iran, and in May, Washington sanctioned three China-based satellite firms for enabling Iran's military operations.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthis seize near control of vital Bab el-Mandeb shipping lane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:463d6e4eae3776ba69b495e9c0970eb80eae5855d7bb1f5945410716a658ddf6</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T20:09:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane--00cc5547baaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels captured the strategic Perim Island in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, located at the southern entrance to the Red Sea, officials said on Friday. The lightning move opens a new front in the Iran war and threatens energy supplies, especially Saudi oil exports, from passing through one of the world's key shipping lanes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis reach strategic island at mouth of vital shipping lane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bc413fcf21786f9ab234f89246aa09785c6a1713f79944010c4fa90ac96f34e</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T19:17:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-reach-strategic-island-at-mouth-of-vital-shipping-lane--9250a7cf8b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-reach-strategic-island-at-mouth-of-vital-shipping-lane" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis took over on Friday a Red Sea island in the middle of the Bab al-Mandeb shipping lane, completing their push to control the area, a local government official and eyewitnesses told AFP. "Boats carrying armed Houthi fighters reached Mayyun Island after government forces withdrew from it yesterday," the official said, referring to an island also known as Perim that divides the strait into lanes. FRANCE 24's Florent Rodo and Rachael Griffiths bring us this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: Tremor recorded as Israel says destroyed key Hezbollah tunnels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e109273987840daa1ccad0f0e8a8033e186fb4de44514ecca8f47047b7382b20</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:14:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-lebanon-tremor-recorded-as-israel-says-destroyed-key-hezbollah-tunnels--7faef7a78e44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-lebanon-tremor-recorded-as-israel-says-destroyed-key-hezbollah-tunnels" /><summary type="html">Israel said Thursday it demolished key tunnels built by the Iran-backed Hezbollah group beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, triggering a 4.1-magnitude tremor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis seize entire Red Sea coast of Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff9f1c47937a9add270a6777d9c4a27e8163a0bcdde4101ce34b24df50e6626</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T04:52:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran--e445beaa418c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels have seized control of the country's entire Red Sea coast, a government official said on Friday. The move inches the rebels closer to gaining near total control of the Bab al-Mandab strait, a vital shipping corridor. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8c7df93122b35c71406882d258b1c6d2a5089a50d9c1768d0815ff59614472</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran--1691e8e9836a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a6bb9b3593391227f5f6eecabdf2d56d51fe2387d7fcb1200be9a995f2000cb</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:50:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake--4867cc6c476d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Thursday it destroyed key tunnels built by Iran-backed Hezbollah beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, completing what it called operational control of the area. Lebanon reported a massive explosion, while the US Geological Survey recorded a magnitude 4.1 tremor nearby.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthi rebels take strategic port city in Yemen, raising threat to Red Sea shipping</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0633baeda9a328df2f0506df4b10a3238a22ab2d29a9109ea2712f052ae27bf2</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping--23593b04e3dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group on Thursday took over Yemen’s port city of Mokha, an area vital to controlling shipping through the Red Sea, Houthi and Yemeni officials said. Mokha is about 80 kilometers (50 miles) from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a waterway that connects the Red Sea and the Gulf of Aden and through which about 12% of the world’s goods are typically shipped. FRANCE 24's Nick Rushworth reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran raises fuel prices for heavy users</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5357c664e52483905c5bd9cd9385266a61ff52afcd5e0f493a3ef0e9109da0cf</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:48:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users--52a75745cc82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users" /><summary type="html">The rise of the price of fuel is an issue for both the United States and Iran in this conflict. US president Donald Trump has conceded that prices will not fall before the midterm elections where the US voters could hold him to account. Meanwhile in Iran where many communities have been bombed since February 28th, there's now the added problem of incresing fuel prices. FRANCE 24's Ali al Basha sent this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli-made film about use of AI for mass killing in Gaza gets record ovation at Venice premiere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdb02013af8850a5c503c7585833725bd717c7cf6b250bc46b442271edb37fc7</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:19:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israeli-made-film-about-mass-killings-in-gaza-gets-25-minute-ovation-at-venice-premiere--0f6192c30bc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israeli-made-film-about-mass-killings-in-gaza-gets-25-minute-ovation-at-venice-premiere" /><summary type="html">A film documenting Israel's use of artificial intelligence to facilitate the mass killing of Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip received a record 25-minute standing ovation at the Venice Film Festival on Thursday. "NAZA" details the brutal Israeli bombardment of the Palestinian territory through anonymous interviews with two dozen whistleblowers from the Israeli military or intelligence services.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
